@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Method / document navigation. Scope-independent process/navigation; provider or runner examples are not MVP prerequisites.
title Resumefolio | Sprint planning and outcome review
skinparam backgroundColor #101827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F1F5F9
skinparam hyperlinkColor #A9D0FF
skinparam dpi 216
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #9FB2CD
skinparam activity {
 BackgroundColor #1C3453
 BorderColor #9FB2CD
 FontColor #F1F5F9
 DiamondBackgroundColor #49351C
 DiamondBorderColor #F2BA72
 StartColor #F1F5F9
 EndColor #F1F5F9
}
start
:Identify authorized work context and reviewed Sprint rules;
if (Authority and required planning conditions met?) then (yes)
 :Define Sprint Goal and select eligible Backlog Items;
 :Identify delivery plan and related tasks under explicit rules;
 :Keep goal + selected items + plan as one Sprint Backlog;
 :Adapt permitted work / plan changes under agreed authority;
 :At the defined end / cancel point, assess actual work conditions;
 if (Completion criteria met for assessed work?) then (yes)
  :Record supported completion / acceptance outcome; <<#173B34>>
 else (incomplete / unmet)
  :Keep incomplete work distinguishable;
  :Record explicit disposition / reselection under reviewed policy; <<#49351C>>
 endif
 :Record Sprint / goal outcome under defined rules;
else (missing / denied)
 :Do not claim valid planning or completion;
 :Record permitted feedback or unresolved policy gate; <<#49351C>>
endif
stop
legend bottom
Conceptual review roadmap, not a final Sprint state machine.
No fixed cadence, automatic carry-over or mandatory ceremony selected.
Task completion and board position alone do not prove item acceptance.
endlegend
@enduml
